window.EN={"1":"Celice and his companions' long journey was finally approaching its last moments.","2":"The Liberation Army's exploits encouraged the people groaning under the Empire's tyranny,","3":"and uprisings broke out among the people in region after region.","4":"First, Silesse returned to the hands of its people,","5":"and then Agustria, answering the Liberation Army's call, rose up in arms as well.","6":"But in the Grannvale homeland itself, still remained","7":"the axe knight corps, the Grauniter, led by Prince Brian of Dozel;","8":"the bow knight corps, the Baigeleiter, led by Prince Scipio of Jungby;","9":"and the thunder knight corps, the Gelpleiter, led by Queen Hilda of Friege —","10":"these elite knight corps were all being held in reserve,","11":"and at Belhalla, Ishtar and the demon prince Julius","12":"kept an uncanny silence, commanding the mysterious Twelve Demon Generals.","13":"More than a year had passed since the uprising in Isaac began,","14":"and the Twelve Crusaders had been split between light and darkness, their tragic battles seeing blood relatives struck down against each other.","15":"And now, the final holy war had begun...","16":"(Julius): So father is dead, is he...","17":"(Manfroy): The emperor was already a useless man. You've saved me the trouble of killing him myself.","18":"(Julius): Heh, father really was a pitiable thing — used and used again by you, and once you had no more use for him, discarded without mercy.","19":"(Manfroy): It was all for Your Highness's sake.","20":"(Manfroy): Lord Arvis, though he inherited the blood of Loptr, opposed the resurrection of the Empire the whole time.","21":"(Manfroy): He carried the temperament of Fala, the flame holy warrior, so strongly that sooner or later, he would have turned against Your Highness.","22":"(Julius): I know that already. By the way, I hear the rebels have reached Chalphy. Is the capital's defense secure?","23":"(Manfroy): Please, rest assured. I've ordered Bishop Rodan of Edda and Prince Brian of Dozel to retake Chalphy.","24":"(Manfroy): There's no need to worry.","25":"(Julius): I see... by the way, how is Julia doing?","26":"(Manfroy): She's held in this castle's dungeon. Someone, bring Princess Julia here!","27":"(Julia): .........","28":"(Julius): Julia, it's been a while. Do you remember me?","29":"(Julia): Brother Julius.........","30":"(Julius): Oh ho, so you do remember. It's already been seven years since you vanished.","31":"(Julia): I've remembered everything. As if it were only yesterday...","32":"(Julius): Hehehe, that's good to hear. Do you remember our kind mother too?","33":"(Julia): ...who are you?","34":"(Julia): At that time... when Archbishop Manfroy brought that eerie black scripture... everything changed completely.","35":"(Julia): My kind brother disappeared forever from that day on,","36":"(Julia): and all that was left was a devil's child with a terrifying power.","37":"(Julia): You took not only mother from me, but my brother too.","38":"(Julia): Just who are you!? Why do you torment us like this!!","39":"(Julius): I am the one who inherits the power of House Loptr, the ruler of this world.","40":"(Julius): Julia, as the one who inherits the power of Naga, my sworn enemy — I must have you die here.","41":"(Manfroy): Please wait, Lord Julius. This girl still has her uses. Leave the rest to me.","42":"(Julius): It seems you've thought of something amusing. Understood, I'll withdraw to Belhalla.","43":"(Julius): I'll leave the rest to you. But don't let your guard down!","44":"(Rodan): By Prince Julius's orders, the warrior-monk and mercenary corps will hold this ground to the death!","45":"(Rodan): The mixed knight corps will retake Chalphy Castle!!","46":"(Levin (Strategist)): This is it, Celice. The final holy war begins.","47":"(Celice): A holy war? Is this really...","48":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right. As a descendant of House Loptr, Julius is plotting to resurrect the dark empire.","49":"(Levin (Strategist)): We must stop him, no matter what it takes.","50":"(Celice): Levin, it seems you know everything about all this.","51":"(Celice): Please, tell me. Just what in the world is going on!","52":"(Levin (Strategist)): I'm sorry, Celice. I apologize for keeping this from you until now.","53":"(Levin (Strategist)): These past ten-odd years, I've traveled in search of the world's truth, and I finally arrived at a great secret.","54":"(Celice): A secret...?","55":"(Levin (Strategist)): Bishop Gale, founder of the Loptr Empire, is said to have crossed the sea in his youth and traveled the world.","56":"(Levin (Strategist)): His purpose was to drink the blood of a certain legendary creature,","57":"(Levin (Strategist)): and obtain a power beyond anything attainable by mere humans.","58":"(Celice): Don't tell me, the blood of the ancient dragon tribe!? But surely that's just superstition!","59":"(Levin (Strategist)): And yet... when Bishop Gale returned from his journey, he possessed a mysterious power.","60":"(Levin (Strategist)): Gale, ambitious by nature to begin with, used that power to indoctrinate young followers,","61":"(Levin (Strategist)): and built up an army of devils who moved entirely at his will.","62":"(Celice): Then what exactly is the dark god Loptous?","63":"(Levin (Strategist)): Probably one of the ancient dragon tribe. And Gale's descendants have inherited that dragon blood ever since.","64":"(Levin (Strategist)): The wicked power of House Loptr is nothing other than the power of the dragon tribe.","65":"(Celice): Then, the holy warriors, our own ancestors...","66":"(Levin (Strategist)): Legend says the gods descended upon the twelve warriors of the Liberation Army at the fortress of Darna.","67":"(Levin (Strategist)): However...","68":"(Celice): However?","69":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, let's save the rest of this for later. Right now, we need to prepare for the enemy's attack.","70":"(Arthur): Tinny, we're almost at mother's homeland, Friege.","71":"(Tinny): Yeah, but I don't have very good memories of it. I imagine it's the same for you, brother.","72":"(Arthur): That's true... House Friege, who took you and mother from me — I've held a grudge against them this whole time.","73":"(Arthur): I wanted to crush them with my own hands.","74":"(Tinny): But you know, uncle Bloom, and Ishtar and brother Ishtore too — they weren't really such bad people.","75":"(Tinny): At least, they were kind to me and to mother.","76":"(Arthur): The one who drove mother to her death was Hilda, wasn't it.","77":"(Tinny): Yeah, that woman alone, I can't forgive. If I could, I wanted to settle it with my own hands...","78":"(Arthur): Tinny, I won't let you feel that sadness anymore. I'll protect you, alright, Tinny!","79":"(Amid): Linda, we're almost at mother's homeland, Friege.","80":"(Linda): Yeah, but I don't have very good memories of it. I imagine it's the same for you, brother.","81":"(Amid): That's true... House Friege, who took you and mother from me — I've held a grudge against them this whole time.","82":"(Amid): I wanted to crush them with my own hands.","83":"(Linda): Say, brother, why did our mother betray her country and join Sigurd's army?","84":"(Amid): Because her close friend, her elder sister, joined Sigurd's army and died in battle.","85":"(Linda): Our aunt?","86":"(Amid): Yeah, someone named Tiltyu, apparently.","87":"(Linda): I see... she died in battle... how sad for her...","88":"— (if Celice is your sweetheart)","89":"(Tinny): Lord Celice...","90":"(Celice): Tinny! Be careful, you mustn't go to the front!","91":"(Tinny): But I want to help too. I want to be of use to you, Lord Celice!","92":"(Celice): But... I don't want to lose you!","93":"(Tinny): I will stay by your side, Lord Celice. I don't want to meet the same fate as Lady Deirdre.","94":"(Tinny): Lord Celice, please — let me stay by your side!","95":"(Celice): I'm sorry, you're right. We mustn't be apart.","96":"(Celice): Tinny, let's go together — I want you to lend me your strength.","97":"(Tinny): Yes! Lord Celice...","98":"— (if Leaf is your sweetheart)","99":"(Tinny): Lord Leaf, are you alright?","100":"(Leaf): Yeah, don't worry about me. You be careful too, Tinny — the enemy here is formidable.","101":"(Tinny): Yes, but as long as you're here with me, I'll be alright.","102":"(Leaf): We have a great task waiting for us — the unification of Thracia. We can't afford to die in a place like this.","103":"(Tinny): Yes, I want to return to Alster too, and work for everyone's sake.","104":"(Leaf): Yeah, but it's not just Alster — you'll need to help me as the queen of the new kingdom of Thracia.","105":"(Tinny): Yes, Lord Leaf!","106":"— (if Sety is your sweetheart)","107":"(Tinny): Lord Sety, are you alright?","108":"(Sety): Yeah, don't worry about me. But you be careful too, Tinny — the enemy here is formidable.","109":"(Tinny): Yes, as long as you're here with me, I'll be alright.","110":"(Sety): Tinny, you're so lovely... my treasure...","111":"(Tinny): ...Lord Sety, when you say things like that, I don't know what to do with myself.","112":"(Sety): Hahaha, sorry. But I wanted to say it while I still could — I'd hate to regret not saying it later...","113":"(Tinny): Lord Sety... please, stay safe...","114":"— (if Celice is your sweetheart)","115":"(Patty): Lord Celice, here, please.","116":"(Celice): Oh, a boxed lunch? Did you make this, Patty? Thank you.","117":"(Patty): Lord Celice, this too.","118":"(Celice): Oh, you even prepared something to drink? You really do notice everything.","119":"(Patty): And while we're at it, this too...","120":"(Celice): Ugh... that's...","121":"(Patty): It's Patty's own handmade energy drink. I'm sure it'll give you energy — drink it all, now.","122":"(Celice): Y-, yeah...","123":"— (if Shanan is your sweetheart)","124":"(Patty): Lord Shanan~","125":"(Shanan): Mm...","126":"(Patty): \"Mm\" isn't an answer — look, a boxed lunch, I made it myself.","127":"(Shanan): You... you act like we're on some kind of picnic.","128":"(Patty): Well, I'm bored, you know — I haven't had much to do lately.","129":"(Shanan): That's no excuse to get in my way. This is a battlefield.","130":"(Patty): Ah, how awful... even you, Lord Shanan, treating me like a burden.","131":"(Patty): And here I put my whole heart into making this lunch... fine, forget it!","132":"(Shanan): Hey, Patty... sorry, I spoke too harshly. Forgive me...","133":"(Patty): So, will you eat the lunch? Really? Ah, I'm so glad... Lord Shanan, I love you!","134":"— (if Lester is your sweetheart)","135":"(Patty): Lester, here!","136":"(Lester): Oh, Patty, I've been waiting — my stomach's so empty I feel dizzy.","137":"(Patty): I thought you'd say that, so I made it extra big today. So, is it good?","138":"(Lester): Delicious! Patty's lunch is the best.","139":"(Patty): Heheh, of course it is!","140":"— (if Dimna is your sweetheart)","141":"(Daisy): Dimna, what are you doing?","142":"(Dimna): Oh, Daisy... I somehow feel empty inside...","143":"(Daisy): Why's that?","144":"(Dimna): Don't you think our presence is kind of thin...","145":"(Daisy): Now that you mention it... we really don't have much of a presence.","146":"(Dimna): Right... I'm going back to my country. I'll just live an ordinary life in Isaac...","147":"(Daisy): Yeah, once this war is over, let's go back together, the two of us. I'm tired too...","148":"(Dimna): We're pretty pathetic, huh...","149":"(Robert): What a prize bounty this is. Sorry, but you'll have to die!","150":"(Robert): Guh... how could this be...","151":"(Boyce): Must I cut down yet another worthless thing...","152":"(Boyce): Ohh... what a terrifying fellow...","153":"(Rodan): Wh-, what is the meaning of this... damn you!","154":"(Rodan): Guh... this too, must be divine punishment...","155":"(Jupheel): Kufufu... foolish humans... become prey to my dark magic!","156":"(Jupheel): Ngh... Lord Julius... forgive me...","157":"(Levin (Strategist)): So this is Edda... if only Father Claud were still alive, he'd surely be pleased...","158":"(Celice): Yes... so Father Claud also died trying to save father. But what of the priest's own child...","159":"— (if Celice is your sweetheart)","160":"(Nanna): Lord Celice...","161":"(Celice): Demaggio, this is a hard battle, but don't push yourself too hard.","162":"(Nanna): Yes, I understand. But I'm worried about you, Lord Celice. Please don't push yourself either.","163":"(Celice): Yeah, but you know, we've come this far — just a little more, let's do our best.","164":"(Nanna): All I can really do is watch over you, but I'll keep praying for you the whole time...","165":"(Celice): Thank you, Demaggio. I can feel your strength. Please, keep watching over me.","166":"(Nanna): Yes, Lord Celice...","167":"— (if Leaf is your sweetheart, Nanna)","168":"(Nanna): Lord Leaf, when will this battle end, I wonder?","169":"(Leaf): Even I don't know that. But one thing is certain — victory is close at hand.","170":"(Nanna): You'll be returning to Leonster, won't you, Lord Leaf?","171":"(Leaf): Yeah, that's my intention. Building a unified nation on this war-torn Thracia Peninsula was my father's dream.","172":"(Leaf): I intend to carry on his will. I want you to be prepared for that too, Demaggio.","173":"(Nanna): Yes, I'll follow you anywhere, Lord Leaf — even to the ends of the earth...","174":"— (if Leaf is your sweetheart, Jeanne)","175":"(Jeanne): Lord Leaf!","176":"(Leaf): Ah, Jeanne. I told you to stay in the castle.","177":"(Jeanne): But...","178":"(Leaf): This battle can only be fought by those with the blood of the holy warriors. It's too much for you.","179":"(Jeanne): I know I'd only be a burden. But surely it's alright if I just use a staff?","180":"(Leaf): I suppose so... but promise me you'll never push yourself too hard. You'll need to help me as the queen of the new kingdom of Thracia.","181":"(Leaf): I'd be in real trouble if you died in a place like this.","182":"(Jeanne): Yes, Lord Leaf...","183":"— (if Ares is your sweetheart, Nanna)","184":"(Nanna): Ares, don't be reckless. You still have a great task ahead of you — rebuilding Agustria.","185":"(Ares): Yeah, I know. I have no intention of dying in a fight like this.","186":"(Ares): I'll carry on my father's will and make Agustria into a splendid nation.","187":"(Nanna): I'm glad, that's just like you, Ares. I'm sure King Eltshan and mother Lachesis would be so pleased.","188":"(Ares): But Demaggio, I can't do it alone. I need your help too.","189":"(Nanna): Of course. I've decided to live my life with you — I won't make the same mistake as my mother.","190":"(Ares): I wonder... did my aunt truly love my father, Eltshan?...","191":"(Nanna): Yes, they were half-siblings, after all — there's nothing so strange about it, is there.","192":"(Ares): Come to think of it, you and I are cousins.","193":"(Nanna): Heheh, that's even less strange, isn't it.","194":"(Mana): Asaello, are you alright? I understand how you feel, but don't push yourself too hard.","195":"(Asaello): If only I had the power of the holy warriors too, I could do so much more... damn it, this isn't fair!","196":"(Mana): Yeah... I think so too, but it's alright, isn't it.","197":"(Mana): We've been doing our best together with everyone, up until now.","198":"(Mana): We have our own pride, as commoners.","199":"(Asaello): Commoners, huh... everyone around us is royalty, nobility... what an unpleasant world, really.","200":"(Mana): That's true... but cheer up! There are so many children back home waiting for you to return.","201":"(Asaello): You're right... this isn't the time to complain... and besides, I have you too, Mana...","202":"(Mana): Heheh, oh, Asaello...","203":"(Philip (purple)): Damn you, I'll knock that head clean off!!","204":"(Philip (purple)): Wh-, what in the world...","205":"(Brian): How dare you kill my father — three generations of House Dozel's grudge, know it well!","206":"(Brian): To think the axe of Swanchika could be defeated this easily... was this really the right thing to do...","207":"(Jupheel): Kufufu... foolish humans... become prey to my dark magic!","208":"(Jupheel): Ngh... Lord Julius... forgive me...","209":"(Levin (Strategist)): Even House Dozel was one of the holy warriors, and yet, what a foolish thing.","210":"(Levin (Strategist)): This too is all Lord Langobalt's responsibility...","211":"(Celice): So then, Levin, who gave the holy warriors their power? Just who exactly were these gods...","212":"(Levin (Strategist)): I don't know for certain, but it seems someone, realizing that this continent's turmoil was caused by the power of the dragon tribe,","213":"(Levin (Strategist)): came from another world to save us.","214":"(Levin (Strategist)): Those beings are said to have suddenly appeared at the fortress of Darna, on the verge of falling.","215":"(Celice): The descent of the goddess Naga and the eleven gods, as told in the scripture.","216":"(Levin (Strategist)): The gods had taken on human form — the light goddess Naga as a young girl, the fire god Salamander as an old man, and so on.","217":"(Levin (Strategist)): And they exchanged a pact of blood with the twelve chosen warriors.","218":"(Celice): A pact of blood?","219":"(Levin (Strategist)): The gods cut their own fingertips, drew blood, and gave that blood to the warriors.","220":"(Celice): !?...","221":"(Levin (Strategist)): In other words, the gods spoken of in the scripture were also of the ancient dragon tribe, just like Loptous.","222":"(Levin (Strategist)): The warriors of the Liberation Army took the dragon tribe's blood into their own bodies, and were reborn as holy warriors.","223":"(Levin (Strategist)): The dragon tribe gave the newborn holy warriors weapons sealed with their own power,","224":"(Levin (Strategist)): and then, leaving behind a few warnings, they departed.","225":"(Celice): So that's how it was... the power of the holy warriors belongs to the dragon tribe...","226":"(Levin (Strategist)): Loptous is the most wicked and terrifying of the dragon tribe.","227":"(Levin (Strategist)): The dragon king Naga gave her own blood to Bishop Heim, the Liberation Army's leader,","228":"(Levin (Strategist)): intending for him to stand against the power of Loptr.","229":"(Celice): In other words, no other dragon tribe member could defeat Loptous?","230":"(Levin (Strategist)): It would be quite difficult, I'd imagine. We would need everyone's combined cooperation, and on top of that, Naga's own power.","231":"(Levin (Strategist)): But... of Heim's descendants, who should have inherited that power, the only ones still alive today","232":"(Levin (Strategist)): are Princess Deirdre's three children.","233":"(Levin (Strategist)): But neither Celice, the first prince, nor Julius, the second prince, have inherited Naga's blood.","234":"(Levin (Strategist)): I've only recently learned that the one who inherited it was Julius's twin sister... Princess Julia, and only her.","235":"(Celice): Wh-, what did you say!?","236":"(Levin (Strategist)): Yes, I didn't realize it myself either, but Julia is Prince Julius's twin sister — and also your own sister...","237":"(Celice): Julia, my sister... that can't be...","238":"(Levin (Strategist)): This solves the mystery of why Julia was captured. Celice, we must save Julia, no matter what it takes.","239":"(Levin (Strategist)): To fight Julius, Julia's power is absolutely essential!!","240":"(Hilda): What did you say! Are you telling me even Dozel has fallen!?","241":"(Hilda): Hmph, every last one of them, utterly spineless. Fine, I'll go out myself.","242":"(Hilda): I'll draw the rebels to this castle and settle the matter in one decisive blow.","243":"(Hilda): Contact Scipio of Jungby. Tell him our Gelpleiter will draw the enemy in,","244":"(Hilda): while Scipio's Baigeleiter strikes from behind.","245":"(Hilda): We'll catch them in a pincer and kill every last one of them!","246":"(Scipio): Heh, the rebels have taken the bait. Alright, cut through the forest and circle around behind the enemy!","247":"(Scipio): Coordinate with the Friege army and surround the enemy!","248":"— (if Celice is your sweetheart)","249":"(Nanna): Lord Celice, just a little further.","250":"(Celice): Yeah, you've done so well too, Nanna. Thank you.","251":"(Nanna): No, I haven't been of any help at all.","252":"(Nanna): But just being at your side, Lord Celice, is enough to make me happy.","253":"(Celice): We've known each other a long time now, Nanna. We've been together ever since we were small.","254":"(Nanna): Yes, we played together so often. Those memories are nothing but joyful ones... but to think it would come to this...","255":"(Celice): But I've liked you, Nanna, ever since I was small.","256":"(Nanna): Lord Celice... when you say things like that, my heart grows weak. I feel so sorry toward Lady Julia...","257":"(Celice): Nanna.........","258":"— (if Scathach is your sweetheart)","259":"(Nanna): Scathach...","260":"(Scathach): Mm...?","261":"(Nanna): You are my pride.","262":"(Scathach): Whoa, what's brought this on so suddenly?","263":"(Nanna): Don't die, Scathach.","264":"(Scathach): Yeah, I can't die and leave you behind.","265":"(Nanna): ...Scathach, I...","266":"(Scathach): Hm?","267":"(Nanna): .........I love you.","268":"— (if Fabal is your sweetheart, Nanna)","269":"(Nanna): Fabal...","270":"(Fabal): Mm...?","271":"(Nanna): You are my pride.","272":"(Fabal): Whoa, what's brought this on so suddenly?","273":"(Nanna): Don't die, Fabal.","274":"(Fabal): Yeah, I can't die and leave you behind.","275":"(Nanna): Fabal, I...","276":"(Fabal): Mm?","277":"(Nanna): .........I love you.","278":"— (if Celice is your sweetheart)","279":"(Lakche): Lord Celice, please wait!","280":"(Celice): Lakche...?","281":"(Lakche): I'm coming with you too!","282":"(Celice): Hm? That's fine, but why?","283":"(Lakche): Somehow, I'm just so frightened...","284":"(Celice): It's unusual for you to say something like that, Lakche.","285":"(Lakche): I...","286":"(Celice): I understand. Let's go together — I feel reassured having you by my side.","287":"(Lakche): Lord Celice...","288":"— (if Shanan is your sweetheart)","289":"(Lakche): Lord Shanan, we've finally made it this far.","290":"(Shanan): Mm, it's been a long road.","291":"(Lakche): I wonder how the people of Isaac are doing right now. I hope nothing's changed for the worse.","292":"(Shanan): Have you started missing home, Lakche?","293":"(Lakche): That's not it at all! I'm not a child anymore, you know!","294":"(Shanan): Is that so? You still look like a child to me.","295":"(Lakche): Lord Shanan!!","296":"(Shanan): Hahaha, don't make such a scary face. It'll ruin that beautiful face of yours.","297":"(Lakche): L-, Lord Shanan...","298":"— (if Johan is your sweetheart)","299":"(Lakche): Johan, are you alright?","300":"(Johan): Even I find it hard to keep up with this fight.","301":"(Johan): But as long as I have your love, I'll endure it, you'll see.","302":"(Lakche): Honestly, you... but, I've fallen in love with you, so there's no helping it...","303":"(Johan): There's no need for regret in love. Lakche, smile and send me off.","304":"(Lakche): Yeah, do your best, Johan.","305":"(Johan): Ah, Lakche...","306":"— (if Johalva is your sweetheart)","307":"(Lakche): Johalva, are you really alright?","308":"(Johalva): Ugh, even I find this fight hard to bear.","309":"(Johalva): But now that we've taken back the Dozel duchy too, I'll try to hold on a bit longer.","310":"(Lakche): Yeah, but don't be reckless. You have a duty to rebuild your country.","311":"(Johalva): Yeah, I know that already.","312":"(Johalva): That's the only way my late old man and brother can rest in peace.","313":"(Johalva): Lakche, you'll help me, won't you.","314":"(Lakche): Yes, you've done so much for me, after all.","315":"(Johalva): Whoa, I'm so grateful. I love you, Lakche!!","316":"(Lakche): Oh, honestly, Johalva, you fool!","317":"(Scipio): My father Andrey's grudge — now, I shall finally avenge it!!","318":"(Scipio): Tch... how could this be...","319":"(Hilda): Hmph, to think I'd be defeated so many times over, it's unbearable!","320":"(Hilda): Guh, how infuriating... Ishtar... avenge this grudge for me...","321":"(Jupheel): Kufufu... foolish humans... become prey to my dark magic!","322":"(Jupheel): Ngh... Lord Julius... forgive me...","323":"(Celice): Levin, we've finally made it to Friege.","324":"(Celice): But I wonder if the children sent to Belhalla are alright. I hope they're safe...","325":"(Levin (Strategist)): Mm, it seems this person wants to speak with us about that very matter.","326":"(Celice): And you are?","327":"(Palmarch (red)): I was a close aide of Emperor Arvis. My name is Felipe.","328":"(Palmarch (red)): In truth, under the emperor's secret orders, I've been sheltering the captured children here in the town of Friege.","329":"(Celice): Eh!? Is that really true! Are all the children safe!!","330":"(Palmarch (red)): Yes, all of them are well, hidden away in the town's convent.","331":"(Celice): But how did they stay safe, with that Hilda ruling over Friege?","332":"(Palmarch (red)): Actually... Princess Ishtar secretly helped us.","333":"(Palmarch (red)): The soldiers feared the princess so much, they couldn't even approach the convent.","334":"(Celice): Princess Ishtar!? But why...","335":"(Palmarch (red)): Lady Ishtar was originally a kind-hearted person.","336":"(Palmarch (red)): For this matter too, she cooperated with us entirely of her own will.","337":"(Palmarch (red)): It was Lady Ishtar herself who led the children out of the Belhalla palace...","338":"(Celice): I see... but I'm glad. Once people learn the children are safe, they'll surely rejoice.","339":"(Celice): Sir Felipe, thank you.","340":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, well done. One of our goals has been achieved — this fight wasn't meaningless after all.","341":"(Celice): Yeah, but Levin, we still haven't found Julia. Where could she be...","342":"(Levin (Strategist)): Mm, if she's not here either, then it must be either the capital Belhalla or Veltomer.","343":"(Celice): Julius is at Belhalla...","344":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right. We must find Julia before we fight him.","345":"(Levin (Strategist)): Without Julia's power, we won't stand a chance.","346":"(Celice): I wonder if Julia can even fight... against her own twin brother, Julius...","347":"(Levin (Strategist)): That... depends entirely on you.","348":"(Ishtar): Then, Lord Julius, I'll take the White Knights and strengthen the capital's defenses.","349":"(Ishtar): Please forgive me for leaving your side for a while.","350":"(Julius): Heh, what's wrong, Ishtar? What are you so flustered about?","351":"(Julius): No matter how many of them come, defeating me is simply impossible. There was no need for you to go out yourself.","352":"(Ishtar): Yes... I understand that well. But I too am a proud mage warrior of House Friege.","353":"(Ishtar): With my parents and siblings killed, I cannot simply go on living shamefully. Please, grant me the chance to fight.","354":"(Julius): You seem to be rushing toward death. Why, Ishtar — have you grown tired of me?","355":"(Ishtar): No... that's not it at all... I love you, Lord Julius...","356":"(Julius): Heheh, well, fine. Fight if you wish to fight — I won't stop you.","357":"(Ishtar): Yes... forgive me. Meng, Breg, Mabel, move out — come with me!","358":"(Meng): Yes ma'am, Lady Ishtar.","359":"(Julius): Then let's settle this all at once. Twelve Demon Generals, you too, move out! Order Arion's mercenary corps to attack as well!","360":"(Julius): Playtime is over. With all our strength, we will finish off the rebels!!","361":"(Manfroy): Fohoho... how noisy it's gotten. Julia, it's your turn. Go finish off those who would defy the Empire.","362":"(Julia (possessed)): Yes... Archbishop Manfroy...","363":"(Arion): We no longer have any home to return to. All troops, follow me.","364":"(Arion): We'll take Chalphy Castle as a foothold to retake our homeland.","365":"(Arion): Show them well the last pride of the Thracian dragon knights!!","366":"— (if Manfroy is still alive)","367":"(Celice): Julia, pull yourself together! What on earth is wrong with you!!","368":"(Julia (possessed)): Kukuku... those who defy Lord Manfroy, all of them, die...","369":"(Levin (Strategist)): No good, Celice, Julia is being controlled by dark magic.","370":"(Levin (Strategist)): Defeat Manfroy first, and then try speaking to her once more!","371":"— (if Manfroy has died)","372":"(Celice): Julia!! Pull yourself together!","373":"(Julia (possessed)): ...","374":"(Julia (possessed)): Hah... Lord Celice!? What... what happened to me?","375":"(Celice): You were under Manfroy's spell, being controlled by him.","376":"(Julia): Manfroy... that's right, I was captured by that man...","377":"(Celice): But I'm so glad, that you're safe.","378":"(Julia): Lord Celice, I...","379":"(Celice): You don't need to say anything more. I've heard everything from Levin.","380":"(Celice): Julia... I'm sorry. If only I'd been stronger...","381":"(Julia): No, this was for the best. I've finally learned, for the first time, the reason I've lived all this time.","382":"(Julia): I will fight. I won't run away.","383":"(Celice): I see... you really are strong, Julia. But you're right.","384":"(Celice): It's a sad fate, but we can't run from it. We mustn't give up, not until the very end.","385":"(Altena): Brother! Enough of this already! Why won't you understand my feelings!!","386":"(Arion): Altena!?","387":"(Altena): Brother, you're a coward! Clinging to pride and appearances, you've lost sight of what truly matters.","388":"(Arion): What do you want me to do?","389":"(Altena): Look at Prince Celice!","390":"(Altena): Think, even just a little, about what he's fighting for, who he's suffering for.","391":"(Arion): You're saying justice lies with Prince Celice...","392":"(Altena): Brother... I can't fight anymore. If you truly won't understand, then defeat me first before you go.","393":"(Altena): If I'm to die by your hand, brother... I have no regrets.","394":"(Arion): Altena... I understand... say no more. I was the one who was wrong...","395":"(Arion): My final work as a mercenary will be for Celice's sake — no, Altena, I'll fight for your sake.","396":"(Altena): Arion... brother.........","397":"— (if Celice is your sweetheart)","398":"(Fee): Lord Celice, shall I go scout the enemy's movements?","399":"(Celice): No, don't be reckless. This battle is different from anything before. Fee, don't leave my side.","400":"(Fee): Yes.........","401":"(Celice): Fee, are you worried about Silesse?","402":"(Fee): Yeah, a little. The fighting must have started there too, I imagine.","403":"(Celice): It seems the people there have risen up. I hear the fighting is going favorably.","404":"(Fee): Really!? Ah, I'm so glad...","405":"(Celice): Do you want to go back to Silesse, Fee?","406":"(Fee): No, not at all! Being by your side, Lord Celice, is the best place for me.","407":"(Celice): I see... thank you, Fee. Having you here makes me feel so much stronger.","408":"(Fee): You're my dream, Lord Celice... I want to stay by your side forever...","409":"— (if Arthur is your sweetheart)","410":"(Fee): Arthur, what are you doing?","411":"(Arthur): What do you mean, what am I doing — I'm fighting, obviously. Must be nice being so carefree, Fee.","412":"(Fee): Well, how rude!","413":"(Arthur): See, you're pouting again already. That's exactly why you...","414":"(Fee): You're going to say I'm not cute, aren't you! How mean!","415":"(Arthur): No, I mean people misunderstand you, that's all. You're cute, Fee — you're precious to me.","416":"(Fee): A-, Arthur... stop it!","417":"(Arthur): Fee, let's be together. Once this war is over, let's go back to Silesse and live together.","418":"(Fee): Arthur... you really mean it... yeah, I'm happy... thank you...","419":"— (if Oifey is your sweetheart, Fee)","420":"(Fee): Mr. Oifey, shall I go scout the enemy's movements?","421":"(Oifey): Fee, don't — you'd be shot down by their archers.","422":"(Fee): Say, Mr. Oifey...","423":"(Oifey): Mm...?","424":"(Fee): I think you're really admirable. You sacrificed your own life, living only for the prince's sake, didn't you.","425":"(Oifey): Mm... in the last war, we survived against our own wishes.","426":"(Oifey): And the mission left to us was something more painful than death itself. That was true for your father and mother too...","427":"(Fee): Lately, I've started to understand, just a little, the way my father and mother chose to live.","428":"(Fee): I was a child. But talking with you, Mr. Oifey, I've started to see so many things.","429":"(Oifey): I see... I was indebted to Lady Fury in the past too. Perhaps I've been able to repay a little of that debt now.","430":"(Fee): Um... Mr. Oifey, please keep teaching me all sorts of things from now on too. I want to become more grown-up.","431":"(Oifey): You don't need to force yourself to grow up so fast. It's fine to become an adult little by little.","432":"(Fee): No! If I do that, you'll end up an old man, Mr. Oifey!","433":"(Oifey): Hey now, Fee...","434":"(Meng): Sorry, but you're going to die!","435":"(Meng): Lady Ishtar, good fortune in battle...","436":"(Meng): .........die!","437":"(Meng): Lady Ishtar... sister...","438":"(Mabel): Take this, my certain-kill blade!!","439":"(Mabel): Lady Ishtar, please forgive me...","440":"(Ishtar): There's nothing left to say... I'll show you the final battle of Ishtar, the Thunder God!","441":"(Ishtar): Lord Julius... I...","442":"(Julia (possessed)): Kukuku.........","443":"(Julia (possessed)): Uugh.........","444":"(Julia): Ahh......... Lord Celice.........","445":"(Arion): Forgive me...","446":"(Arion): Ngh... Altena...","447":"(Manfroy): How foolish... everything I've built over my entire lifetime... ngh, I will not forgive you!!","448":"(Manfroy): Lord Julius... please, the Loptr Empire, I beg you...","449":"(Celice): Levin, is it true that the Scripture of Naga is hidden in this castle?","450":"(Levin (Strategist)): Yes, it seems Emperor Arvis took it from the Belhalla palace and hid it here.","451":"(Levin (Strategist)): Isn't that right, Sir Felipe?","452":"(Palmarch (red)): Yes, it should be in this treasury. But it can't be opened without the key.","453":"(Levin (Strategist)): The key, you say? Where is that?","454":"(Palmarch (red)): The emperor had the key fitted into the circlet, Queen Deirdre's keepsake.","455":"(Palmarch (red)): If only we had that circlet, we could open it...","456":"(Levin (Strategist)): Queen Deirdre's circlet...","457":"(Levin (Strategist)): Julia, this is the treasury. Try holding the circlet's ornament against that hollow there.","458":"(Julia): Yes...","459":"(Levin (Strategist)): It opened, just as I thought... ah, there it is! This is the Scripture of Naga!! Julia, here, take it!","460":"(Julia): So this is... ahh, I feel such a strange sensation.","461":"(Julia): Something so nostalgic somehow... a warm feeling...","462":"(Julius): Hehehe... have you lost your senses? A mere thing like you could never defeat me.","463":"(Julius): Gwaaaaaaaaaaaah","464":"(Elder): Descendants of the brave, let me recite for you the poem of the holy warriors.","465":"(Elder): ~ The Black Knight Hezul, with the cursed blade Mystletainn, cleaves through the darkness,","466":"(Elder): the Holy Swordsman Od, with the holy sword Balmung, drives away the darkness,","467":"(Elder): the Holy Knight Baldr, with the holy sword Tyrfing, illuminates the darkness,","468":"(Elder): and finally, the saint Heim, with the Scripture of Naga, prays to the heavens.","469":"(Elder): That prayer becomes light, and the light becomes a white dragon, challenging the dark dragon to battle.","470":"(Elder): The white dragon and the black dragon, light and darkness, a long battle with no end in sight,","471":"(Elder): leading to either victory, or death.","472":"(Elder): But I shall not fear, even should our battle end in defeat.","473":"(Elder): The light we sought shall never be lost.","474":"(Elder): I believe in those who will carry on our hearts.","475":"(Elder): I believe in those who will carry on our light ~","476":"(Elder): How was that, quite a pleasant ring to it, wouldn't you say?","477":"(Elder): Brave ones, descendants of the holy warriors — whether this battle is a true holy war or not rests entirely in your hands.","478":"(Elder): Throw everything — all the strength and courage you've gathered until now — into this battle.","479":"(Elder): And believe that your future lies where those two lights shine!"};
